# Recording state truth

- Capture owns exactly one symbol. Serialize start/stop through the capture worker.
  Starting the active symbol is idempotent; starting another or stopping a different
  symbol returns HTTP 409 without stopping/replacing the active recorder.
- `/api/ibkr/status` must reconcile recorder self-stop before exposing capture fields.
  Capture errors are logged and returned as `capture_error` alongside those fields.
- The existing IBKR status poller owns recording freshness. A client Record click
  requests a refresh; it never optimistically adds/removes symbols. Persisted cache,
  failed polls and snapshots older than 15 seconds cannot claim active recording.
  Subscribers must receive expiry updates even when the next request hangs.
- Tab recording never suppresses Gateway login or API/wedged-loop prerequisites;
  recording needs those services too. Runtime order gates remain unchanged.
- Record/Stop failures stay visible in the symbol menu. Cover ownership conflicts,
  backend restart/self-stop, failed/hung polling, fresh recovery, and visible errors.
- Use feature modules under ADR 001; no new runtime loop or market-data owner.
